 persistence begins with foundational comprehension, the policy introduces Dialogic Reading Protocols in lower-secondary language arts classrooms. These structured, interactive discussion routines deepen reading comprehension and critical reasoning, reducing early dropout risk and creating the literacy scaffolding necessary for advanced coursework.\n\nTogether, these four candidate interventions form a coherent theory of change: dialogic reading and active teaching methods improve the daily learning experience and reduce dropout; blended learning adds flexibility for those at risk of leaving school; and STEM pathways build the academic capital and institutional familiarity that drive tertiary enrollment. Each lever maps directly to evidence-backed mechanisms in the candidate lever space, ensuring the policy remains grounded in observable, context-bound educational interventions.",
